    "narrative": "The anchor of today\u2019s lineup is **Taylor Ward**, who earns an elite score of 71.19, the only player to cross the 70-point threshold. His matchup against Noah Cameron is ideal; **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a significant platoon advantage, making him our primary offensive catalyst. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier are **Bryce Harper** (61.09) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.77). **Bryce Harper** maintains high value despite a tough matchup against Casey Mize, buoyed by his excellent 0.396 xwOBA and a favorable spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Gavin Sheets** draws a generous 13% boost from his matchup against Trey Yesavage, showcasing the type of SP skill exploitation we are prioritizing to maximize our daily efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Geraldo Perdomo**, who landed just outside the cut at 47.83. While his spot in the batting order provided a +8% lift, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a -15% penalty against the elite arm of Yoshinobu Yamamoto. We prioritized the higher efficiency of **Masyn Winn** and **Tyler Freeman** to manage our game caps more effectively. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Dylan Beavers**, both of whom benefit from the park factor at their venue today; however, **Dylan Beavers** carries a risk flag due to his L/L platoon disadvantage against Noah Cameron. With all lineups currently pending, these projections assume historical order placements, and any movement down the lineup for players like **Cal Raleigh** or **Yainer Diaz** could further dampen their already marginal scores, forcing us to remain agile as the day progresses.",
